WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.827
Testing CSP starts with ordinary browser
developer tools.

2
00:00:04.907 --> 00:00:09.321
The console can show blocked resources,
policy violations,

3
00:00:09.401 --> 00:00:12.344
and useful details during development.

4
00:00:12.424 --> 00:00:18.655
Staging environments should run policies
that closely match production so teams can

5
00:00:18.735 --> 00:00:23.063
catch missing sources and unsafe patterns
before release.

6
00:00:23.143 --> 00:00:29.028
Automated header checks can verify that
key pages include expected CSP headers,

7
00:00:29.108 --> 00:00:32.051
but header presence alone is not enough.

8
00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:36.977
The policy content and the application
behavior both need review.

9
00:00:37.057 --> 00:00:40.346
Template and script usage review is
central.

10
00:00:40.426 --> 00:00:45.273
Look for inline scripts, inline event
handlers, raw HTML helpers,

11
00:00:45.353 --> 00:00:48.728
dynamic script loading, tag manager
changes,

12
00:00:48.808 --> 00:00:54.001
and places where framework escaping or
binding patterns are bypassed.

13
00:00:54.081 --> 00:00:59.880
Regression testing should include pages
with authentication, payment flows,

14
00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:06.105
embedded widgets, dashboards, file
previews, and other frontend-heavy features.

15
00:01:06.185 --> 00:01:12.156
A policy that works only for the homepage
may not protect the application where the

16
00:01:12.236 --> 00:01:13.448
risk is highest.

17
00:01:13.528 --> 00:01:15.086
CSP needs ownership.

18
00:01:15.166 --> 00:01:19.147
Someone should understand why each
directive exists,

19
00:01:19.227 --> 00:01:24.247
why each source is allowed, when
report-only findings are reviewed,

20
00:01:24.327 --> 00:01:26.491
and how changes are approved.

21
00:01:26.571 --> 00:01:32.369
Document policy decisions so future
developers do not weaken the policy to fix a

22
00:01:32.449 --> 00:01:36.084
broken page without understanding the
tradeoff.

23
00:01:36.164 --> 00:01:40.665
As applications change, the CSP should
evolve deliberately.

24
00:01:40.745 --> 00:01:42.909
Maintenance is not busywork;

25
00:01:42.989 --> 00:01:48.008
it is what keeps a once-useful policy from
becoming outdated, noisy,

26
00:01:48.088 --> 00:01:49.300
or overly broad.
